# RepliKam fleet provisioning — copy to fleet.conf, fill in, NEVER commit fleet.conf.
#
# KEY-AT-CLAIM (M10): there is NO tailnet auth key here any more. The card ships
# without a tailnet key; the key is delivered once when an admin claims the device
# in the panel. A lost card is therefore not a live tailnet key.
#
# CONTROL_URL — where a freshly flashed bridge enrolls. This is the ONE thing that
# must be right for key-at-claim to work:
#   ⚠️ It MUST be reachable by a bridge that is NOT yet on the tailnet — i.e. a
#      PUBLIC https:// URL. A tailnet address (100.x) or localhost will deadlock:
#      the bridge can't reach the control plane to get the key that would put it
#      on the tailnet. (Stand up a public HTTPS endpoint — e.g. `tailscale serve`
#      /a reverse proxy with a real cert — and point this at it.)
CONTROL_URL=https://fleet.YOURDOMAIN.example
# From ~/Downloads/fleet-admin-credentials.txt (BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN line). Authorizes
# ONLY enrollment; rotate server-side (settings.bootstrap_tokens) without reflashing.
BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN=REPLACE_ME
BRIDGE_VERSION=2.0.0
